1
00:00:00,148 --> 00:00:03,179
Flash a torch at your friend, and
you've just built the internet.

2
00:00:03,219 --> 00:00:05,539
That's all it is: light,
blinking on and off.

3
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:07,251
On is one. Off is zero.

4
00:00:07,591 --> 00:00:08,918
Eight blinks make one letter.

5
00:00:09,321 --> 00:00:10,767
But hello takes forty blinks.

6
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:12,308
Too slow.

7
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,400
So we use a wire.

8
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:15,664
Now it's a billion blinks, every second.

9
00:00:16,194 --> 00:00:17,498
Hello arrives before you blink.

10
00:00:18,131 --> 00:00:20,308
Then she moves to a hostel. New wire.

11
00:00:20,649 --> 00:00:22,452
Then a friend's place. Another wire.

12
00:00:22,492 --> 00:00:24,058
Now the neighbours want to join too.

13
00:00:24,098 --> 00:00:25,848
So every house plugs into one box:

14
00:00:26,199 --> 00:00:26,899
the router.

15
00:00:27,038 --> 00:00:29,017
Every house gets a number,
like a door number.

16
00:00:29,517 --> 00:00:30,590
That's its IP address.

17
00:00:30,957 --> 00:00:32,954
The router reads the number
and delivers the message.

18
00:00:33,326 --> 00:00:35,135
Then she moves to another city.

19
00:00:35,781 --> 00:00:37,618
One router can't reach that far.

20
00:00:37,658 --> 00:00:39,259
So routers connect to other routers,

21
00:00:39,798 --> 00:00:41,692
and pass the message along, hop by hop.

22
00:00:42,978 --> 00:00:45,622
A text is tiny. But what about a photo?

23
00:00:45,662 --> 00:00:48,760
Imagine sending it as one big
piece. It blocks the whole line.

24
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,378
Everyone else has to wait.

25
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:52,962
One small error, and
it has to start again.

26
00:00:53,002 --> 00:00:55,013
So the internet never
sends it in one piece.

27
00:00:55,169 --> 00:00:58,147
It cuts the photo into about two
thousand small pieces, called packets,

28
00:00:58,328 --> 00:00:59,808
each with her address and a number.

29
00:01:00,223 --> 00:01:01,950
They share the wires with everyone else.

30
00:01:02,283 --> 00:01:04,066
Wire busy? Some take another path.

31
00:01:04,186 --> 00:01:06,322
One lost? Only that one is sent again.

32
00:01:06,622 --> 00:01:08,147
And her phone puts them back in order.

33
00:01:08,808 --> 00:01:10,356
Then she flies to London.

34
00:01:10,396 --> 00:01:12,380
Next: how a photo crosses an ocean.

35
00:01:12,817 --> 00:01:14,270
Follow InvisiTech for more.
